br.br:
1. A bidirectional incentive spirometer for connection to and use with pulmonary treatment and drug delivery devices, comprising:
a linear, hollow cylindrical body, having an exterior surface, a distal end port and a proximal end port, said body defining a linear cavity therebetween said distal end port and said proximal end port for the flow a gas pulse;
at least one motion sensor having a sensing element operationally positioned between said distal end port and said proximal end port within said body so as to detect a flow of said gas pulse, a direction of gas pulse along an interior passage of said body;
a battery affixed to said body;
a microprocessor with a real time clock and a memory, said microprocessor affixed to said body;
a cycle initiation switch extending from said body;
wherein said battery, said microprocessor and said cycle initiation switch are in operative communication with said motion sensor to collect data, said data including a date and time of the occurrence of a flow of said gas pulse and a direction of said flow of said gas pulse within said linear cavity when said motion detector experiences a motion due to said flow of said gas pulse within said linear cavity.
2. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 1 further comprising:
a wireless transceiver for the transmission of said data, said wireless transceiver affixed to said body and connected to said microprocessor.
3. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 1 further comprising:
a data collection port connected to said microprocessor.
4. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 1 wherein said motion sensor is selected from the group of motion sensors including Hall effect sensors, heated anemometers, bidirectional resistive strain sensors, flexible diaphragm pressure switches, swing make or break contact switches, pivotable fibers or strands, bidirectional accelerometers, IR radio frequency beam sensors and the functional equivalents, alone or in combination thereof.
5. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 2 wherein said motion sensor is selected from the group of motion sensors including Hall effect sensors, heated anemometers, bidirectional resistive strain sensors, flexible diaphragm pressure switches, swing make or break contact switches, pivotable fibers or strands, bidirectional accelerometers, IR radio frequency beam sensors and the functional equivalents, alone or in combination thereof.
6. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 3 wherein said motion sensor is selected from the group of motion sensors including Hall effect sensors, heated anemometers, bidirectional resistive strain sensors, flexible diaphragm pressure switches, swing make or break contact switches, pivotable fibers or strands, bidirectional accelerometers, IR radio frequency beam sensors and the functional equivalents, alone or in combination thereof.
7. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 5 further comprising:
a data collection port connected to said microprocessor;
a battery housing affixed to said exterior surface said body, said battery residing therein said battery housing;
an LED light;
an external housing affixed to said body, wherein said microprocessor, said wireless transceiver, said LED light, said cycle initiation switch and said data collection port are housed therein said external housing
8. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 7 wherein said motion sensor is directly coupled to said external housing and integrated with said microprocessor.
9. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 1 wherein said proximal end port is a 15 mm ID female port and the distal end port is a 22 mm OD male port.
10. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 1 wherein said data also comprising a duration of said occurrence of said flow of said gas pulse based on a length of time when said motion detector experiences a motion due to said flow of said gas pulse within said linear cavity.
11. A bidirectional incentive spirometer for connection to and use with pulmonary treatment and drug delivery devices, comprising:
a linear, hollow cylindrical body, having an exterior surface, a distal end port and a proximal end port, said body defining a linear cavity therebetween said distal end port and said proximal end port for the flow a gas pulse;
at least one motion sensor having a sensing element operationally positioned between said distal end port and said proximal end port within said body so as to detect a flow of said gas pulse, a direction of gas pulse along an interior passage of said body;
a battery affixed to said body;
a microprocessor with a real time clock and a memory, said microprocessor affixed to said body;
a magnetic cycle initiation switch operationally connected between said battery and said microprocessor;
a motion activated accelerometer switch operationally connected between said battery and said microprocessor;
wherein said battery, said microprocessor, said cycle initiation switch and said accelerometer switch are in operative communication with said motion sensor so as to collect data, said data including a date and time of the occurrence of a flow of said gas pulse and a
direction of said flow of said gas pulse within said linear cavity when said motion detector experiences a motion due to said flow of said gas pulse within said linear cavity.
12. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 11 further comprising:
a wireless transceiver for the transmission of said data, said wireless transceiver affixed to said body and connected to said microprocessor.
13. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 11 further comprising:
a data collection port connected to said microprocessor.
14. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 11 wherein said motion sensor is selected from the group of motion sensors including Hall effect sensors, heated anemometers, bidirectional resistive strain sensors, flexible diaphragm pressure switches, swing make or break contact switches, pivotable fibers or strands, bidirectional accelerometers, IR radio frequency beam sensors and the functional equivalents, alone or in combination thereof.
15. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 12 wherein said motion sensor is selected from the group of motion sensors including Hall effect sensors, heated anemometers, bidirectional resistive strain sensors, flexible diaphragm pressure switches, swing make or break contact switches, pivotable fibers or strands, bidirectional accelerometers, IR radio frequency beam sensors and the functional equivalents, alone or in combination thereof.
16. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 13 wherein said motion sensor is selected from the group of motion sensors including Hall effect sensors, heated anemometers, bidirectional resistive strain sensors, flexible diaphragm pressure switches, swing make or break contact switches, pivotable fibers or strands, bidirectional accelerometers, IR radio frequency beam sensors and the functional equivalents, alone or in combination thereof.
17. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 15 further comprising:
a data collection port connected to said microprocessor;
a battery housing affixed to said exterior surface said body, said battery residing therein said battery housing; and
an external housing affixed to said body, wherein said microprocessor, said wireless transceiver, said cycle initiation switch and said data collection port are housed therein said external housing.
18. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 17 wherein said motion sensor is directly coupled to said external housing and integrated with said microprocessor.
19. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 11 wherein said proximal end port is a 15 mm ID female port and the distal end port is a 22 mm OD male port.
20. The bidirectional incentive spirometer of claim 11 further comprising an LED light connected to said microprocessor to visually indicate when said motion sensor senses motion; and
wherein said data also comprises duration of said occurrence of said flow of said gas pulse based on a length of time when said motion detector experiences a motion due to said flow of said gas pulse within said linear cavity. 1 2 3 4 5 6 7
